  "notes": [
    "Two WAVES bands on one seed, so the lobes line up. The outline layer is wound wider - amplitude 0.34 against 0.24, starting at 0.52 against 0.60 - and painted first, so what survives at the fringe is a thick cartoon lip. The gap works out well over a body unit at the bottom of each lobe, which is the minimum that reads at half a unit per texel.",
    "BODY only. A Y band on the pitched NECK is a collar and not a topline stripe, so the drips stop at the withers rather than trying to run down the throat. If they should carry onto the neck, that is a second layer in space local, not a wider parts list."
  ]
